1. EXPRESSIVE SPEECH & FIRST AMENDMENT PROTECTION
In accordance with established judicial precedent including Bernstein v. U.S. 
Department of Justice, 176 F.3d 1132 (9th Cir. 1999) and Junger v. Daley, 209 F.3d 481 
(6th Cir. 2000), software source code, metadata schemas, and parsers constitute expressive 
speech protected under the law. The distribution of technical constructs, parser manifests, 
and user-agent scripts is an exercise of protected technical speech.

2. REVERSE ENGINEERING & INTEROPERABILITY FAIR USE
This Software is designed solely to facilitate interoperability between media playback 
clients (CloudStream 3, Nuvio) and publicly available hypertext markup. In accordance with 
17 U.S.C. § 107, 17 U.S.C. § 1201(j) (Security & Interoperability Exemption), and the rulings 
in Sega Enterprises Ltd. v. Accolade, Inc., 977 F.2d 1510 (9th Cir. 1992) and Sony Computer 
Entertainment, Inc. v. Connectix Corp., 203 F.3d 596 (9th Cir. 2000), intermediate parsing 
and architectural modeling for the sole purpose of achieving interoperability with public 
endpoints is lawful and non-infringing.

3. ABSOLUTE ABSENCE OF MEDIA HOSTING (SAFE HARBOR)
The Software acts purely as a client-side parser, equivalent to a web browser, RSS reader, 
or hypermedia indexer. Under no circumstances does this repository, its maintainers, or its 
associated network nodes host, cache, transmit, duplicate, or distribute any video streams, 
audio files, audiovisual works, MP4/M3U8 containers, or copyrighted multimedia assets. All 
stream resolution is executed dynamically on the end-user's device against third-party servers. 
Pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 512 (DMCA Safe Harbor) and Directive 2000/31/EC of the European Parliament, 
the authors maintain complete neutral intermediary status.

4. INDEMNIFICATION & ACCEPTABLE USE
The Software is provided for private research, accessibility enhancement, and format 
standardization only. Users of the Software assume full and exclusive responsibility for 
compliance with applicable local, national, and international laws. By using the Software, 
the user agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the authors, developers, and 
contributors from any claims, damages, liabilities, or expenses arising from the end-user's 
deployment, streaming behavior, or third-party interactions.

5. DISCLAIMER OF ALL WARRANTIES ("AS-IS")
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, 
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR 
